{"id": "P0266", "style": "", "text": "Single SB Cabinet D&D Movement", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0267", "style": "", "text": "I left a comment earlier stating that when a single SB cabinet is in the scene, the countertop should move with the cabinet. I’d like to clarify this further: the action described above should occur when a thin top is used, because it doesn’t support remote or offset cabinet placement/compositions.", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0268", "style": "", "text": "In the recording they whole configuration moves as one unit.", "links": ["https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1JvFpY9Ks34NuNMMXjpxpCyIPiqrRqx6l"], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0269", "style": "", "text": "However, when a thick countertop is used, there should be two movement classification patterns", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0270", "style": "", "text": "5.1 or 5.5” thick tops - the SB cabinet should be allowed to move freely", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0271", "style": "", "text": "1) If the SB cabinet remains in contact with the countertop, the cabinet would remain an SB, and the integrated basin or vessel hole cutout would reposition itself to where the SB cabinet is located", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0272", "style": "", "text": "", "links": [], "images": ["media/image33.png"], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0273", "style": "", "text": "", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0274", "style": "", "text": "2) If the SB cabinet is moved remotely, it would change to an SC cabinet, and the integrated basin or vessel hole cutout would remain in place (the countertop always needs one)", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0275", "style": "", "text": "", "links": [], "images": ["media/image23.png"], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0276", "style": "", "text": "", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0277", "style": "", "text": "4” thick tops - SB can only move laterally (4” tops cannot be offset or remote), and the integrated basin or vessel hole cutout would reposition itself to where the SB cabinet is located", "links": [], "images": [], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
{"id": "P0278", "style": "", "text": "", "links": [], "images": ["media/image9.png"], "comments": [], "heading": ""}
